The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-22-integrated-benchmark-operator-approved-plan.txt|approved implementation direction]] requires all executable deployment helpers in AI4R, an easy shared local/SSH command path and seven-day expiry of owned temporary resources only. Inputs, retained results, credentials, models and durable app/lab state are protected. Actual Spark testing is deferred; complete independent local checks and report unrun host checks. See [[Activities/2026-10-22 Integrated Benchmark Operator]] for the implemented code location and current validation.

## Nuwa correction: preserve presentation principles, rebuild the subject

The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-23-nuwa-person-to-skill-and-orange.txt|latest correction]] explicitly rejects filling the Paper2Agent talk as a template. Nuwa takes a person and produces a person-perspective skill. The [[Designs/Nuwa Briefing/presentation/README|orange revision]] now starts there, shows the person-specific layers and a Karpathy example, then connects the skill to existing AI4R reasoning steps, shortcomings and a bounded comparison. This supersedes the earlier factory-first narrative and visual palette while retaining a short, diagram-led talk. It does not change architecture or assert measured benefit.

## Nuwa rev3: AI4R value is the central question

The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-23-nuwa-ai4r-methodology-and-luna.txt|latest steering]] clarifies that AI4R is the point, not an optional connection. [[Designs/Nuwa Briefing/presentation/README|Rev3]] asks what Nuwa and its methodology can teach AI4R: source-linked procedure extraction, explicit failure conditions, disagreement, research directions and stronger checks. It adds a separate proposed M2 CC-factory pipeline slide and retains Nuwa's person-to-skill explanation. The user explicitly requested Luna adversarial review; its critiques led to conditional value claims, an untested-example label, separate qualification/admission and a generic-checklist control. This supersedes the interim optional-context framing, without adopting an implementation or claiming measured benefit.

