The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-23-nuwa-value-second.txt|approved reorder]] moves the former AI4R-value slide 5 into position 2, shifts former 2–4 to 3–5, and preserves the remainder. [[Designs/Nuwa Briefing/presentation/README|Rev3]] retains all content, orange design, notes and 6:40 timing. This is a presentation-order change only.

## Nuwa methodology as a third factory interface

The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-23-nuwa-method-detail-three-factory-inputs.txt|latest direction]] requests concrete tables of mental models, decision rules, research sources and criteria, centered on methodology useful to AI4R. [[Designs/Nuwa Briefing/presentation/README|The revised rev3]] replaces its two broad explanation slides with those tables and presents three intended CC-factory inputs: a capability gap observed during a run; paper/repository/data; and a person name plus a target trait. These are distinct entry interfaces into one proposed lifecycle, with route-specific diagnosis, reproduction or research before shared candidate authoring, qualification and admission. A name/trait starts evidence discovery, and a gap starts diagnosis; neither proves a useful capability or grants promotion. This refines the earlier Nuwa-only branch into a shared interface view without claiming deployed interfaces or changing maintained runtime contracts.

## Nuwa pipeline order and explicit value answer

The [[Sources/Prompts/2026-10-23-nuwa-pipeline-order-explicit-value.txt|latest direction]] puts source exploration before the models/rules it produces. [[Designs/Nuwa Briefing/presentation/README|Rev3]] now gives a direct answer on slide 2: yes, useful as an evidence-backed capability-authoring design pattern. This is an assessment of design utility; measured AI4R task gains remain unproven. Research is slide 3, extraction slide 4; all later order and planned 7:20 timing remain.

## Nuwa scope correction, 2026-10-23

The latest direction narrows Nuwa's contribution to human-to-skill research/extraction as a possible person-plus-trait factory input. It supersedes the presentation's broader evidence-backed capability-authoring endorsement. AI4R retains its own capability evidence, tests and admission. Nuwa's small persona-fidelity evaluation and permissive structural checker do not establish task capability. This is presentation/design intent, not implementation or an empirical comparison of the systems.
